+# Coupled status
+
+Inspect a recorded native coupled run without provider calls, tool execution, API keys, or file changes:
+
+```text
+spiral coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+The installed npm entry forwards the same command and arguments:
+
+```text
+npx spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+`--run-dir` is required. Relative paths resolve from the caller's current working directory. The command reads `iterations.json` and durable `state/tui-work.json` ledgers only. `wire` counts every durable request; `task` counts requests charged to the task, including the native default when `charge` is omitted. Failed and in-flight requests are counted rather than inferred from logs.
+
+Interrupted pending usage may be unknown when its ledger has not been written. In that case the pending counts and aggregate used/remaining values are `null`, while declared limits remain known; unknown usage is never treated as zero. A recorded `status` of `completed` describes the native manifest record, not independent verification or promotion authorization.
+
+The following is the completed synthetic example from `scripts.status_fixture.make` and is the measured expected result:
+
+```json
+{"version":1,"status":"completed","stop_reason":"completed","iterations":[{"iteration":1,"task_id":"t1","termination":"completed","task_requests":2,"wire_requests":3,"changed_files":["src/a.rs"],"newly_verified":["cargo test -q"]}],"pending":null,"requests":{"task_used":2,"wire_used":3,"task_limit":192,"wire_limit":216,"task_remaining":190,"wire_remaining":213}}
+```
